{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05XM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$2$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}'/\\mathcal{Y}') \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y}) \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\mathcal{Y}' \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{Y}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$2$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-map-hilbert}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-cartesian-map-hilbert}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a8c42bce4ed341a853e13fbb11b63c223f10c046665dcd8a9bae35cc5df4bb25", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fbdb07aac648a8dc81d345717594417af19ea5a373ee8d2d3bf134ffb47753c3", "source_text": "In the situation of\nLemma <REF_0001>\nassume that the given square is <MATH_0001>-cartesian. Then the diagram\n<MATH_0002>\nis <MATH_0003>-cartesian.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fa3694cb5e5b09c98b849e7d0ae5baabf5d11087d51f1019c8858fb67233da1f", "unit_id": "tag:05XP:statement"}
{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05XM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$2$", "MATH_0002": "$1$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}'/\\mathcal{Y}')\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{Y}' \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y})\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$y'$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{Y}'_U$", "MATH_0008": "$(U, Z, y, x, \\alpha)$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}/\\mathcal{Y})$", "MATH_0010": "$U$", "MATH_0011": "$H(y') \\to y$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{Y}_U$", "MATH_0013": "$x'$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{X}'_Z$", "MATH_0015": "$G(x') \\cong x$", "MATH_0016": "$\\alpha' : y'|_Z \\to F'(x')$", "MATH_0017": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0018": "$(U, Z, y', x', \\alpha')$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{H}_d(\\mathcal{X}'/\\mathcal{Y}')$", "MATH_0020": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-map-hilbert}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e479d5585cf0096b456ccb41be9744e3ceb30d38de8a31c641552783026028c1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c24891d4d1652a6e34f5b489fc75837277ac2d669438f2f779c6f054b2740a65", "source_text": "We get a <MATH_0001>-commutative diagram by\nLemma <REF_0001>\nand hence we get a <MATH_0002>-morphism (i.e., a functor)\n<MATH_0003>\nWe indicate why this functor is essentially surjective. Namely, an object\nof the category on the right hand side is given by a scheme <MATH_0004> over <MATH_0005>,\nan object <MATH_0006> of <MATH_0007>, an object <MATH_0008>\nof <MATH_0009> over <MATH_0010> and an isomorphism\n<MATH_0011> in <MATH_0012>. The assumption means exactly that\nthere exists an object <MATH_0013> of <MATH_0014> such that there exist\nisomorphisms <MATH_0015> and <MATH_0016> compatible\nwith <MATH_0017>. Then we see that <MATH_0018> is an\nobject of <MATH_0019> over <MATH_0020>.\nDetails omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7d43f10b5167fae472db86ab1b58f3a7a8898995c59eb02d7faf54df97dcee05", "unit_id": "tag:05XP:proof"}
